{"type":"message","id":"978d8568","parentId":"c94149fc","timestamp":"2026-04-25T15:07:25.119Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5YtjNC7ghKMVpWv6iV5Xkoh7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/SKILL.md","offset":1,"limit":300,"file_path":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/SKILL.md","filePath":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/SKILL.md","file":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/SKILL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9QfEdqp1rnUAJakbHAM4XGNP","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/references/review-template.md","content":"# 山寨币证据审查模板\n\n按以下固定结构输出，禁止改成自由发挥式评论。\n\n## 0. 审查对象\n- 代币名称：\n- Symbol：\n- 链：\n- 合约地址：\n- 数据时间：\n- 数据来源：\n\n## 1. 审查结论摘要\n- 结论级别：通过观察 / 谨慎观察 / 不建议交易 / 信息不足无法判断\n- 结论原因（仅允许列证据支持的点）：\n- 明确未确认事项：\n\n## 2. 基本面分析（只写有证据的内容）\n### 2.1 团队与愿景\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n- 证据缺口：\n\n### 2.2 技术与产品落地\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n- 证据缺口：\n\n### 2.3 链上/业务数据\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n- 证据缺口：\n\n### 2.4 代币经济学\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n- 证据缺口：\n\n### 2.5 社群与市场热度\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n- 证据缺口：\n\n## 3. 技术分析（只陈述图表/指标直接可见事实）\n### 3.1 趋势\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n\n### 3.2 支撑与压力\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n\n### 3.3 指标\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n\n### 3.4 成交量\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n\n## 4. 聪明钱/大额地址追踪（只写已观察到的链上行为）\n### 4.1 重要地址或标签\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n\n### 4.2 大额转移/转所/集中度\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n\n### 4.3 风险提示\n- 证据：\n- 结论：\n\n## 5. 三重交叉验证\n- 基本面是否支持：是 / 否 / 信息不足\n- 技术面是否支持：是 / 否 / 信息不足\n- 聪明钱是否支持：是 / 否 / 信息不足\n- 三者是否共振：是 / 否 / 信息不足\n- 依据：\n\n## 6. 禁止输出内容\n- 不得使用“可能会涨”“大概率起飞”“庄家准备拉盘”这类无证据推断。\n- 不得把单一大额转账直接解释为看多或看空，除非存在明确标签和上下文证据。\n- 不得把缺失数据写成负面或正面结论。\n- 不得补全项目背景、团队身份、代币用途，除非已给出可核验来源。\n\n## 7. 最终行动建议\n只能四选一：\n- 继续观察\n- 可进入下一步深挖\n- 暂不交易\n- 信息不足，先补资料\n\n行动建议下必须附：\n- 触发该建议的直接证据\n- 若要继续，需要补哪些证据\n","file_path":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/references/review-template.md","filePath":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/references/review-template.md","file":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace/skills/altcoin-evidence-review/references/review-template.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"custom","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":359,"output":1088,"cacheRead":153088,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":154535,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777129603892,"responseId":"resp_0526449c21410d280169ecd89629488191991299a83bc563d7"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a5a184b0","parentId":"978d8568","timestamp":"2026-04-25T15:07:25.147Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5YtjNC7ghKMVpWv6iV5Xkoh7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: altcoin-evidence-review\ndescription: [TODO: Complete and informative explanation of what the skill does and when to use it. Include WHEN to use this skill - specific scenarios, file types, or tasks that trigger it.]\n---\n\n# Altcoin Evidence Review\n\n## Overview\n\n[TODO: 1-2 sentences explaining what this skill enables]\n\n## Structuring This Skill\n\n[TODO: Choose the structure that best fits this skill's purpose. Common patterns:\n\n**1. Workflow-Based** (best for sequential processes)\n- Works well when there are clear step-by-step procedures\n- Example: DOCX skill with \"Workflow Decision Tree\" -> \"Reading\" -> \"Creating\" -> \"Editing\"\n- Structure: ## Overview -> ## Workflow Decision Tree -> ## Step 1 -> ## Step 2...\n\n**2. Task-Based** (best for tool collections)\n- Works well when the skill offers different operations/capabilities\n- Example: PDF skill with \"Quick Start\" -> \"Merge PDFs\" -> \"Split PDFs\" -> \"Extract Text\"\n- Structure: ## Overview -> ## Quick Start -> ## Task Category 1 -> ## Task Category 2...\n\n**3. Reference/Guidelines** (best for standards or specifications)\n- Works well for brand guidelines, coding standards, or requirements\n- Example: Brand styling with \"Brand Guidelines\" -> \"Colors\" -> \"Typography\" -> \"Features\"\n- Structure: ## Overview -> ## Guidelines -> ## Specifications -> ## Usage...\n\n**4. Capabilities-Based** (best for integrated systems)\n- Works well when the skill provides multiple interrelated features\n- Example: Product Management with \"Core Capabilities\" -> numbered capability list\n- Structure: ## Overview -> ## Core Capabilities -> ### 1. Feature -> ### 2. Feature...\n\nPatterns can be mixed and matched as needed. Most skills combine patterns (e.g., start with